# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GTS Algo Research — SUPERVISED LIVE TEST: 1 LOT PER LEG, 4-WIDE CONCURRENCY
#
# Derived from deploy/supervised-live-test.env.template. Read that file too — its
# per-variable traps still apply and are not all repeated here.
#
# ── READ THIS FIRST: WHAT "4 CONCURRENCY" CAN AND CANNOT MEAN ────────────────
# Four concurrent Box ENTRIES are IMPOSSIBLE in this system, by design, and no
# environment variable changes that. src/box/executionSchedulingPolicy.ts, in
# `admitBoxOperation`, refuses a second Box pipeline unconditionally and BEFORE
# any slot arithmetic:
#
#     if (occupancy.entryAttemptId !== null &&
#         occupancy.entryAttemptId !== request.attemptId) → refuse
#     "a second Box pipeline may never overlap it, so contract reservations
#      cannot be bypassed"
#
# So raising BOX_LIVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS to 4 does NOT buy four
# simultaneous entries. What 4-wide concurrency really means here is:
#
#   BOX_LIVE_ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY=4  → the FOUR LEGS OF ONE BOX may be in
#                                          transport simultaneously. This is the
#                                          real 4-wide axis, and the one that
#                                          matters: it shrinks the window in
#                                          which the box is partially legged and
#                                          therefore UNHEDGED.
#   BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=4            → up to four boxes may be HELD open at
#                                          once. They are still ENTERED ONE AFTER
#                                          ANOTHER, never concurrently.
#
# This file configures the first of those (4 legs concurrent, 1 lot each) and
# leaves the second at 1 for the first run, with the exact deltas for going to
# four open boxes in §11.
#
# ── LOT SIZE: THE SHIPPED TEMPLATE IS STALE ──────────────────────────────────
# deploy/supervised-live-test.env.template documents NIFTY as 75. NSE revised
# index F&O lot sizes for the January 2026 contracts; NIFTY is now 65 units.
#   · https://algotest.in/blog/nifty-lot-size/  (65, effective Jan 2026 series)
#   · https://www.bajajfinserv.in/nse-and-bse-lot-size-increase  (NIFTY 65,
#     BANKNIFTY 30, SENSEX 20)
#   · https://www.icicidirect.com/futures-and-options/articles/revised-quantity-freeze-limits-for-nse-index-derivatives
#     (revised lot size 65 → effective freeze quantity 1,755)
# Content above was rephrased for compliance with licensing restrictions.
#
# You do NOT set the traded quantity here. It is read from the broker instrument
# master (src/kite.ts parses `lot_size` from the Zerodha instruments dump), and
# src/box/singleLotInvariant.ts independently refuses the entry unless all four
# legs share one lot size and each fill equals EXACTLY one lot. The variables
# below are CEILINGS. Set them to the lot size the instrument master actually
# reports on the day — confirm it, do not trust any table, including this one.
#
# ── VERIFY WHAT IS IN FORCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#     node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js
# The integer loader turns a blank, unparseable or out-of-range value into the
# DEFAULT, silently. Read the effective-config output; do not eyeball this file.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. THE THREE LIVE GATES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three are independent on purpose: no single stray variable arms live.
# `live` without BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true is REJECTED AT BOOT.
#
# ⚠ Set BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=live only at the moment of the supervised attempt,
#   with an operator watching, and revert it immediately afterwards. Arming the
#   session (§3) is still a separate, deliberate human action after boot.
BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=live
BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true
ZERODHA_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true
# If testing on Dhan instead, set ZERODHA_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=false and:
# DHAN_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true
# DHAN_STATIC_PUBLIC_IP=<your whitelisted egress IP>

BOX_SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=false             # shadow can never place an order
BOX_PAPER_EXECUTION_PROFILE=standard      # `stress` is rejected in live


# ── 2. THE 4-WIDE AXIS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE point of this profile. All four legs of the one box may be in transport at
# once, so first-to-last submit is no longer bounded below by three complete
# order lifecycles.
BOX_LIVE_ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY=4       # clamped to 1..4; 4 = all four legs

# BASE lifecycle concurrency. Deliberately left at 1, NOT raised to 4.
#
# WHY 1 IS BETTER THAN 4 HERE. Entry admission takes BASE slots greedily before
# it bursts, and protective work (PROTECTIVE_CANCEL / EXIT / EMERGENCY_RESIDUAL)
# is admitted against BASE occupancy ONLY. With base=4 all four entry legs occupy
# all four base slots, so protective work waits for one of four lifecycles to
# finish. With base=1, exactly one leg holds base and legs 2-4 ride burst slots —
# so the base slot frees after ONE leg resolves and a protective operation can
# start while three legs are still in flight.
#
# The burst also only opens when burstWidth > base, so base=4 with burst=4 would
# report "adds no headroom" and collapse this profile back to plain base
# concurrency. base=1 + burst=4 is the configuration that actually gets four
# legs moving while keeping the fastest possible path to getting flat.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS=1

# Wire pacing is a SEPARATE mechanism from lifecycle concurrency: brokerPacing.ts
# throttles order mutations regardless of how many lifecycles overlap. The burst
# makes four legs READY to transmit; this interval still spaces them.
# 250 ms ⇒ 4 orders/sec ⇒ ~750 ms across four legs, comfortably inside Zerodha's
# order-placement limit. Lower it to 150 to shrink the unhedged window further
# only after a paper run at 150 has been observed clean.
BOX_LIVE_BROKER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=250


# ── 3. THE ONE-ATTEMPT BOUND ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMPLETED_TRADES bounds SUCCESS (consumed when a full four-leg box is
# established). ENTRY_ATTEMPTS bounds RISK-TAKING (consumed at ADMISSION, before
# any broker POST) — this is the one that stops a trial "configured for one
# trade" from submitting indefinitely while no attempt ever completes.
BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES=1
BOX_SESSION_MAX_ENTRY_ATTEMPTS=1
#
# ⚠ 0 MEANS UNLIMITED, and a malformed value BECOMES 0. `=one` and `=-1` both
#   mean UNLIMITED ATTEMPTS.
#
# ⚠ RE-ARM IS REQUIRED. Both ceilings are snapshotted into the session row when
#   the session is armed. Editing this file and restarting does NOT rebind an
#   already-armed session. Arm a FRESH session after this env is in place, or
#   pass them explicitly:
#
#     POST /api/box/session/arm
#     { "max_completed_trades": 1, "max_entry_attempts": 1 }
#
#   Then CONFIRM the status endpoint reports max_entry_attempts: 1 and
#   remaining_entry_attempts: 1.


# ── 4. ONE BOX, ONE UNDERLYING, NO RESIDUAL TOLERANCE ────────────────────────
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=1                 # ⚠ 0 does NOT mean unlimited — the
                                          #   guard is `openBoxes >= limit`, so
                                          #   0 means NO box may ever open.
BOX_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_UNDERLYING=1
BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING=true    # code default is false — ON here.
                                          #   This is the limit that counts
                                          #   partial, residual, recovering and
                                          #   in-flight exposure, and it is what
                                          #   blocks a second attempt on the same
                                          #   underlying after an abort. It also
                                          #   survives a restart, because it is
                                          #   derived from durable state, not a
                                          #   lease.

BOX_LIVE_MAX_RESIDUAL_LEGS=0              # ⚠ comparison is STRICTLY GREATER
                                          #   (`residualLegs > limit`), so the
                                          #   code default of 1 TOLERATES one
                                          #   unresolved residual leg. 0 is the
                                          #   only value that blocks on the first.

BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS=1                     # 0 = no cap. 1 for this test.
BOX_STRIKE_LEVEL=3                        # ATM ±3 (clamped to 1|2|3); enough
                                          #   distinct strike pairs to find a box


# ── 5. ONE LOT PER LEG — CEILINGS, NOT THE ORDER SIZE ────────────────────────
# Set to the lot size the instrument master reports. 65 = one NIFTY lot on the
# January-2026-onward contracts. Do NOT round these up "to be safe": they are the
# last defence against a size mistake.
#
#   Instrument   1 lot   4-leg gross (4 × lot)
#   ──────────   ─────   ─────────────────────
#   NIFTY           65                     260
#   BANKNIFTY       30                     120
#   SENSEX          20                      80
#
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=65         # per leg — exactly one NIFTY lot
BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=260  # 4 legs × 65, process-wide aggregate
#
# WHY GROSS MUST BE ≥ 4 × LOT. The whole four-leg envelope is checked BEFORE the
# first leg posts (orderManager.ts, `committedByOthers + quantityPerLeg * legs`).
# Setting gross below 4 × lot does not cap the box smaller — it makes the attempt
# IMPOSSIBLE, and the refusal names this variable. Set it below and legs 1-2 used
# to reach the broker before leg 3 was refused, acquiring real hedge exposure
# against a cap the attempt could never satisfy.
#
# GROSS IS PROCESS-WIDE. It counts other attempts and pre-existing positions in
# FULL, netting out only the current attempt's own reservations. Because the
# comparison is strictly `>`, the number is self-enforcing: 260 admits exactly one
# 1-lot NIFTY box and refuses a second concurrently.


# ── 6. FUNDING GATES — ALL ARMED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three default to FALSE in code. All three ON here: MISSING or STALE
# evidence then REFUSES the entry instead of assuming the account can bear it.
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_FUNDS_COVER=true
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_MARGIN_EVIDENCE=true
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_STAGE_FUNDING=true
#
# WHY STAGE FUNDING IS NOT REDUNDANT. For Zerodha the basket margin's headline
# total is the FINAL figure — the margin AFTER the spread benefit of a COMPLETED
# box, i.e. the cheapest moment in the sequence. MARGIN_EVIDENCE alone can be
# satisfied by a number far below what the intermediate legging window requires.
# STAGE_FUNDING forces the initial/final split apart and requires every stage of
# the real hedge-first sequence to be fundable. With four legs in flight at once
# this matters MORE, not less.

BOX_LIVE_FUNDS_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000
BOX_LIVE_MARGIN_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=2500    # a stalled broker endpoint cannot hold
                                          #   an admission decision open
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_CONCURRENT_READS=false  # serial; the broker's rate limiter is
                                          #   the authority on whether overlap is
                                          #   safe


# ── 7. CAPITAL CAP AND RECOVERY RESERVE — ⚠ 0 MEANS DISABLED ─────────────────
# Both default to 0, and at every enforcement site 0 means "no opinion". A config
# with both at 0 is UNCAPPED and UNRESERVED. The cap is GROSS OPTION-ORDER
# NOTIONAL — not margin, not peak exposure, not max loss.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_BOX_CAPITAL_RUPEES=100000    # EDIT: your approved per-box cap
BOX_LIVE_RECOVERY_RESERVE_RUPEES=25000    # EDIT: rupees withheld to fund the
                                          #   cancel/unwind that recovers a
                                          #   partially legged box


# ── 8. MARKET-DATA FRESHNESS AND FOUR-LEG COHERENCE ──────────────────────────
BOX_QUOTE_MAX_AGE_MS=15000                # per-leg book age
BOX_FEED_MAX_AGE_MS=5000                  # whole-universe feed liveness
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_RECEIVE_DISPERSION_MS=500    # PRIMARY live coherence gate
BOX_MAX_RECEIVE_TO_EXCHANGE_DELAY_MS=5000
BOX_COHERENCE_ZERO_DISPERSION_DISABLES_IN_LIVE=false   # in LIVE, 0 is
                                          #   impossible-to-satisfy, NOT a bypass

# ⚠ RAISED FROM THE 250 THE OTHER TEMPLATE SHIPS. Kite's order-book timestamp is
#   whole-SECOND granular, so any limit below 1000 ms can reject four genuinely
#   coherent books on quantisation alone. 250 fails SAFE (it refuses entries, it
#   never admits an incoherent one) but in practice the attempt may simply never
#   be admitted, and `cross_leg_time_skew` is the refusal you would see. 1000 is
#   the documented Zerodha-appropriate value (see
#   deploy/mumbai-ec2-conservative.env.example). The receive-time gate above
#   (500 ms) remains the primary live gate and is unaffected by exchange-stamp
#   granularity. Decide this BEFORE the window, not mid-attempt.
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_EXCHANGE_DISPERSION_MS=1000


# ── 9. ORDER-UPDATE STREAM — ARMED FOR THIS PROFILE ──────────────────────────
# Zerodha order updates arrive as TEXT frames on the existing box quote socket;
# there is no separate order socket to open.
ZERODHA_ORDER_STREAM_ENABLED=true
#
# ⚠ COUNTER-INTUITIVE. `false` is the PERMISSIVE setting for entry: REST polling
#   is the documented baseline, so a disabled stream does not block entry, it only
#   makes fill observation slower. ARMING it makes entry STRICTER — a CONNECTING /
#   RECONCILING / DEGRADED / DISCONNECTED stream then REFUSES new entry.
#
#   It is armed here BECAUSE this profile puts four legs in flight at once. That
#   is exactly the situation where slow fill observation is most expensive: the
#   sooner a fill on leg 1 is seen, the sooner an unhedged partial is detected and
#   unwound. The cost is that a half-connected stream will refuse the attempt
#   outright. That is the correct trade for a supervised run — but do NOT read a
#   `DEGRADED` refusal as a fault. If you would rather the attempt not be hostage
#   to stream health, set this to false; REST reconciliation remains the fill
#   authority either way and cannot double-count against the stream.


# ── 10. ECONOMIC GATE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BOX_MIN_EXPECTED_NET_PROFIT=1200          # expected net profit after every cost
BOX_REQUIRE_PRICED_CHARGES=true           # never admit on unpriced charges


# ── 11. BROKER TOKEN TIMERS — NEVER LEAVE THESE BLANK ────────────────────────
# Set explicitly and with valid values. A PRESENT-but-blank or malformed value
# used to defeat the timer it configures: `BROKER_TOKEN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=`
# became 0 and aborted every token fetch (costing the whole trading day's token,
# reported only as an ordinary timeout), and `BROKER_TOKEN_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=`
# became 0 and turned the retry schedule into an unbounded request loop against
# the token provider. Both are now validated and warn on rejection, but set them
# correctly regardless.
BROKER_TOKEN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
BROKER_TOKEN_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
BROKER_TOKEN_POLL_START=09:00


# ── 12. RUN 2 ONLY — UP TO FOUR OPEN BOXES ───────────────────────────────────
# Do NOT apply this until run 1 above has completed cleanly, flat, with the
# reconciliation and P&L surfaces agreeing. Entries remain SEQUENTIAL; this only
# permits four boxes to be HELD at once.
#
# Replace the §4/§5 values with:
#   BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=4
#   BOX_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_UNDERLYING=4
#   BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING=false   # ⚠ REQUIRED for >1 box on ONE
#                                             #   underlying — and it REMOVES the
#                                             #   guard that blocks a re-entry
#                                             #   while a residual is unresolved.
#                                             #   BOX_LIVE_MAX_RESIDUAL_LEGS=0 is
#                                             #   the compensating control; keep it.
#   BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=1040 # 4 boxes × 4 legs × 65. Strictly
#                                             #   `>`, so 1040 admits exactly four
#                                             #   and refuses a fifth.
#   BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES=4
#   BOX_SESSION_MAX_ENTRY_ATTEMPTS=6          # 4 completions + 2 aborts
#   BOX_LIVE_RECOVERY_RESERVE_RUPEES=100000   # scale the reserve with open boxes
#
# PREFERRED ALTERNATIVE: keep BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING=true and spread
# the four boxes across FOUR DIFFERENT underlyings (BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS=4). That
# retains the residual guard. The cost is that
# BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY is a single global number, so it must be set to
# the LARGEST lot size in the set, which loosens the per-leg cap for the smallest.


# ── 13. PRE-ATTEMPT CHECKLIST (all must be confirmed, in order) ──────────────
#  1. `node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js` shows every ceiling above as EFFECTIVE —
#     in particular ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY=4 and MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS=1.
#  2. The instrument master's `lot_size` for your underlying EQUALS
#     BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY. If NSE has revised it again, this file is
#     stale — fix it before arming.
#  3. PostgreSQL connected and migrations applied, including
#     011_order_intent_broker_account.sql. Without it live order persistence fails.
#  4. Broker signed in AND the account is named: identity.account_present: true
#     and account_masked non-null. Otherwise live entry is refused as "the broker
#     account could not be identified" — NOT as a token problem. Re-login through
#     the in-app flow populates it.
#  5. Static IP confirmed out-of-band against the API key. For Zerodha
#     static_ip_configured is null = NOT MODELLED, which does not mean not
#     required.
#  6. Market data READY with ticks_observed: true (not merely a connected socket)
#     and a non-empty universe.
#  7. Order stream CONNECTED — §9 arms it, so a DEGRADED stream will refuse entry.
#  8. reconciliation_complete: true, zero unknown orders, breaker closed, no
#     residual legs, recovery not active.
#  9. A FRESH session armed with both ceilings, verified as in §3.
# 10. An operator watching the position and P&L surfaces with the abort procedure
#     below open in front of them.
#
# ── ABORT PROCEDURE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exposure reduction is INDEPENDENT of the entry controls: turning entry off does
# NOT disable getting flat. In order of escalation:
#   1. Disarm the session          → no further attempt is admitted.
#   2. box_entry_enabled = false   → no NEW exposure. Cancel, exit and attributed
#                                    reduction all continue.
#   3. Cancel working orders       → explicit result: 409 with a reason if
#                                    refused, 207 with per-order failures on a
#                                    partial sweep. It cannot report empty success.
#   4. Exit / flatten the attributed box position.
#   5. Revert BOX_EXECUTION_MODE to paper_latency and restart.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
